This proof works for those morphisms of quasi-compact and quasi-separated schemes such that $Rf_*P$ is pseudo-coherent for all $P$ perfect on $X$. It follows easily from a theorem of Kiehl <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Kiehl">Kiehl</a>]</span> that this holds if $f$ is proper and pseudo-coherent. This is the correct generality for this lemma and some of the other results in this chapter.